    "type_designations": ["LI-700E", "HC5600"],
    "description": "Self-indicating and price-computing non-automatic weighing instrument operating as a weight or weight/price labeller with associated thermal label printer. Construction: stainless steel frame; scale conveyor with optional in-feed and out-feed conveyors (any number); labeller; control cabinet located behind the conveyors. Devices: initial zero-setting device, semi-automatic zero-setting device, zero-tracking device, preset tare device, semi-automatic tare device (subtractive), zero indication; calibration not accessible to user; price computation; PLUs. Interfaces: Ethernet, USB. Software: version 2.xx.xx.xxxx displayed during power-up; alternatively World View software (permitted for direct sales to the public); legally relevant software contained in HeaderDisplay.dll version 1.0.0.10 and DPS710.dll version 1.0.0.29. HC5600 variant: identical in construction to the LI-700E, using the Tesco Counter application software (version 3.2.1) with DPS700.dll (checksum 0D37) and Secure.Scale.Module/dll (checksum 73954ba292858692bd28349bf20cda33e6a26a) to perform checkweighing; Max = 3000 g, Min = 40 g, e = 2 g. Any compatible load cell(s) with an OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity may be used, subject to compatibility of modules established by the manufacturer at the time of verification."
